                <pb facs="0839" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg727"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Whitehouse to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1891-10-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                    1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Whitehouse telegraphs that the restrictions against such hog products as may
                    he accompanied by health certificate have been removed by the Government of
                    Italy. He states that live pigs are not included, the decree being still in
                    force against their importation.</p>
            </div>
